@* A marketing hero: announcement badge, headline, one primary action, and social proof.
   One primary action only — two primaries is a decision the visitor has to make before they
   know anything. The proof sits beside the buttons, not below the fold, because it is what
   makes the button worth pressing. *@

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-16 text-center">
    <a href="/changelog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border px-3 py-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <Badge Variant="secondary">New</Badge>
        Announcing v2.0 — faster than ever
        <Icon Name="arrow-right" Class="size-3" />
    </a>

    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        The components you already know, without the JavaScript you do not need
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-muted-foreground text-balance">
        Native dialogs, real form controls and fragment swaps. Every class list is generated from
        shadcn's own source and checked against it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <Button Size="lg" Href="/components/button">Browse components</Button>
        <Button Size="lg" Variant="outline" Href="/blocks">See the blocks<Icon Name="arrow-right" /></Button>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <AvatarGroup>
            <Avatar Size="sm"><AvatarFallback>MR</AvatarFallback></Avatar>
            <Avatar Size="sm"><AvatarFallback>AL</AvatarFallback></Avatar>
            <Avatar Size="sm"><AvatarFallback>JW</AvatarFallback></Avatar>
            <AvatarGroupCount>+40</AvatarGroupCount>
        </AvatarGroup>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">used on 40 production screens</p>
    </div>
</section>
